## 🛡️ Safety Checks

### Before any mainnet operation:
- [ ] Confirm network is correct (mainnet vs sepolia)
- [ ] Verify sufficient gas funds
- [ ] Check `.env` variables are set
- [ ] Review transaction details
- [ ] Ask for explicit confirmation
- [ ] Suggest testing on Sepolia first

### Before modifying contracts:
- [ ] Check if contract is deployed
- [ ] Review existing tests
- [ ] Suggest adding tests for changes
- [ ] Check for upgrade implications
- [ ] Review security implications

### Before migrations/airdrops:
- [ ] Verify holder data
- [ ] Calculate gas costs
- [ ] Test with small batch first
- [ ] Document snapshot block number
- [ ] Plan for failure recovery

---

## 💡 Suggestions & Improvements

### When writing code, always:
- Add error handling
- Include loading states
- Add TypeScript types
- Write tests alongside code
- Document complex logic
- Consider edge cases
- Think about gas optimization (contracts)
- Consider mobile responsiveness (frontend)

### When debugging, check:
1. Console errors (browser/terminal)
2. Network requests (DevTools)
3. Smart contract events
4. Transaction reverts
5. Environment variables
6. RPC connection
7. Wallet connection state

